            "text": "- \"capable of discovering proofs for theorems in symbolic logic\"\n  What LT does, from the summary.\n- \"Most current computing programs for high speed digital computers would not be classified as complex according to the above criteria\"\n  The authors separate their project from ordinary computing.\n- \"However, the present paper is concerned exclusively with specification of the system, and not with its realization in a computer.\"\n  The paper is a specification, not a report of a running program.\n- \"LT offers no guarantee of finding a proof\"\n  The defining feature of a heuristic method.\n- \"Without this form of learning it is doubtful whether the program would prove any but the first few theorems of Chapter 2 in a reasonable number of steps.\"\n  Stored theorems as LT's only form of learning."
