        "keyClaim": "SRI and the IEEE present Shakey as the first mobile robot able to perceive and reason about its surroundings. Built at Stanford Research Institute's Artificial Intelligence Center from 1966 to 1972, it could, in the IEEE citation's words, \"perceive its surroundings, infer implicit facts from explicit ones, create plans, recover from errors in plan execution, and communicate using ordinary English.\" The IEEE nomination argues that its layered software, vision, planning and navigation methods became models for later robots and for consumer technology.",
