        "citation": "Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency. 1983. Strategic Computing (program plan presented to Congress). October 1983. https://apps.dtic.mil/sti/citations/ADA138274",
        "keyClaim": "DARPA's Strategic Computing program set out to reach machine intelligence by advancing a whole research front at once. Salisbury describes the plan as a pyramid: microelectronics and computer architecture at the base, AI applications for the military in the middle, and generic machine intelligence at the top, all driven by large gains in computing power from linking many processors. Between 1983 and 1993 DARPA spent over $1 billion on it. Salisbury's verdict is that the program \"over-promised and under-delivered\" and faded into obscurity by the early 1990s, while producing narrower successes.",
