        "keyClaim": "The builders' own account describes Deep Blue as a massively parallel search system: a general-purpose IBM supercomputer combined with hundreds of custom chess chips, able to evaluate hundreds of millions of positions per second. The paper presents its win as the result of specialized hardware, search, and a hand-tuned evaluation function, not as a machine that \"thinks\" about chess the way people do.",
