        "keyClaim": "LeCun and colleagues at AT&T Labs-Research argue that pattern recognition systems improve when they rely more on automatic learning and less on hand-designed heuristics. They make the case in two steps. First, on a new benchmark of handwritten digits, MNIST, convolutional neural networks that learn their own features from pixels beat every other method they test. Second, whole document-reading systems can be trained end to end with Graph Transformer Networks instead of being assembled from separately designed modules. The paper ends in a deployed product: a check reader built around LeNet-5 that reads millions of checks.",
