        "citation": "Waymo. n.d. \"Company\" (Waymo History timeline, entry for 2009: \"The Google self-driving car project begins\"). Waymo. Accessed September 25, 2026. https://waymo.com/company/",
        "keyClaim": "Waymo's company history dates its origin to 2009, when Google set itself the challenge of driving autonomously over ten uninterrupted 100-mile routes in Toyota Prius cars. Google's first public account of the project came in Sebastian Thrun's October 2010 blog post. It presents self-driving cars as a way to prevent traffic accidents, free up commuting time and cut emissions \"by fundamentally changing car use,\" and reports that the test cars, always with trained operators on board, had logged over 140,000 miles. Waymo's current page tells the same history as the first steps toward a commercial product: \"the world's most trusted driver.\"",
