            "text": "- Relevant Social Groups: Pichai names the audience as \"everyone from academic researchers, to engineers, to hobbyists,\" and Dean and Monga add institutions \"no matter where you work.\" Each group gets something different: researchers get shared code, engineers get production deployment, Google gets a wider pool of people trained on its system.\n- Interpretative Flexibility: Pichai says TensorFlow \"is for more than just machine learning\" and could help with protein folding or astronomy data. Google presents the tool as open to many uses while it is still defining what it is.\n- The framing of ownership: Dean and Monga write that \"the most important thing about TensorFlow is that it's yours.\" The license gives users rights to the code, while Google keeps the development team, the roadmap and the internal production use. The note records this as Google's rhetoric of openness, not as a transfe"
