            "text": "- Before: NVIDIA CUDA (2006) made GPUs programmable for general computing; Google's release assumes GPU training as the normal starting point (\"training on your desktop GPU\").\n- Before: ImageNet Classification with Deep Convolutional Neural Networks (2012) and the ImageNet challenge; DistBelief trained the Inception model that won the 2014 challenge.\n- After: Google Duplex demo (2018) was built using TensorFlow Extended.\n- After: PyTorch 1.0 released (2018) is Facebook's competing framework, which also claims to span research and production."
