            "text": "This paper was written about machine translation. Its tables are BLEU scores on WMT English→German and English→French. The word \"language model\" is not its subject, and nothing in it proposes the use the architecture is now famous for.\n\nThe transformer became the substrate of general-purpose LLMs through later reinterpretation by other groups, not through its designers' intent.\n\nThat is the cleanest case in this vault of Kline + Pinch's central claim, and it is worth writing into the note explicitly:\n\n> a stabilised artifact can become flexible again when it enters a new community, a new environment, a new system of labour, or a new set of social relationships — “Users as Agents of Technological Change”\n\nHere the \"users\" are other researchers, and the \"misuse\" — stripping the encoder, scaling the decoder, and training on undifferentiated web text — produced the product category."
