            "text": "- Interpretative Flexibility at the Use Stage — what the transformer is for was decided after it existed. Translation architecture → general sequence model → foundation for GPT-3.\n- Restabilization — the architecture stabilised a second time, around a different function, without a corresponding redesign. Kline + Pinch's term for exactly this.\n- Black Box — the transformer block is now so stable that papers cite it without describing it. Its earlier uncertainty (was recurrence really droppable?) has been forgotten, which is Kline + Pinch's definition.\n- \"Scaling Laws for Neural Language Models\" — dropping recurrence made training parallel across sequence positions, which made the scaling regime economically reachable. The architectural choice and the capital story are the same story.\n- Technological Momentum — once GPU kernels, libraries, inference servers, hiring pipelines, and hardware "
