            "html": "<p>MLPerf's founders argue that machine learning needs industry-standard benchmarks to compare the fast-growing number of hardware and software systems for training neural networks. The May 2018 launch announces a suite that measures the time it takes to train models to perform tasks such as recognizing objects, translating languages and playing Go. The 2020 paper explains why this is harder than earlier computing benchmarks: speed-ups can lower model quality, training is random, and systems differ so much that identical code and settings are hard to impose. MLPerf answers with a &quot;time to train&quot; to a fixed quality target, reference implementations, and rules about what submitters may change.</p>",
