        "citation": "ACLU of Northern California. 2019. \"San Francisco Board of Supervisors Approves Historic Face Surveillance Ban and Oversight Law.\" Press release. May 14, 2019. https://www.aclunorcal.org/press-releases/san-francisco-board-supervisors-approves-historic-face-surveillance-ban-and-oversight-law/",
        "keyClaim": "On May 14, 2019, the San Francisco Board of Supervisors passed the Stop Secret Surveillance Ordinance, authored by Supervisor Aaron Peskin. The ACLU of Northern California and the coalition behind the law present it as doing two things: bringing \"accountability and oversight to surveillance technology\" in general, and making San Francisco \"the first city in the United States to prohibit government use of face surveillance systems.\" The coalition argues that face recognition in government hands would expand state power to track people, \"supercharge discriminatory policing,\" and entangle residents with immigration enforcement, and that the right answer is democratic control before adoption rat",
