            "text": "The OECD Council adopted its Recommendation on Artificial Intelligence at its ministerial meeting on May 22, 2019, calling it \"the first intergovernmental standard on AI.\" The Recommendation sets out five values-based principles for \"responsible stewardship of trustworthy AI\" (inclusive growth and well-being; rule of law, human rights and democratic values; transparency and explainability; robustness, security and safety; accountability) and five recommendations to governments (R&D investment, an enabling ecosystem, an interoperable policy environment, labour-market preparation, international co-operation). Its premise is that trust is what lets AI spread: the Council treats trustworthiness as \"a key factor for the diffusion and adoption of AI.\" The cached text is the 2024 revision, so the principle wording quoted below is the current version, not necessarily the 2019 wording."
