        "citation": "Torralba, Antonio, Rob Fergus, and William T. Freeman. 2020. \"80 Million Tiny Images\" (withdrawal notice). MIT Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Laboratory. June 29, 2020. https://groups.csail.mit.edu/vision/TinyImages/ (archived copy via the Wayback Machine).",
        "keyClaim": "On June 29, 2020, the creators of the 80 Million Tiny Images dataset at MIT withdrew it. Their notice says the dataset \"contains some derogatory terms as categories and offensive images,\" a result of \"the automated data collection procedure that relied on nouns from WordNet.\" Because the images were too many and too small to inspect by hand, they decided removal was the only reliable fix: the dataset was taken offline for good, and they asked researchers to stop using it and delete their copies. The notice credits a preprint by Vinay Prabhu and Abeba Birhane, which argued that large vision datasets inherited offensive categories from WordNet and were built from images of people collected wit",
