        "citation": "OpenAI. 2021. \"CLIP: Connecting Text and Images.\" OpenAI Blog. January 5, 2021. https://openai.com/index/clip/ Source used for this note: Internet Archive copy of the original post at https://openai.com/blog/clip/",
        "keyClaim": "OpenAI announces CLIP (Contrastive Language–Image Pre-training), a model that learns visual concepts from text paired with images found on the internet rather than from hand-labeled datasets. Because it is trained to match images with captions, CLIP can be turned into a classifier for almost any set of categories by naming them in plain language, with no task-specific training examples. OpenAI argues that this makes CLIP's benchmark scores more honest: a model that never trains on a benchmark cannot \"cheat\" on it, so its performance there better predicts its performance elsewhere.",
