            "id": "core-claim",
            "title": "Core Claim",
            "html": "<p>The Commission proposes binding EU-wide rules for AI systems, built on a risk tier rather than a technology definition: certain practices are prohibited outright, &quot;high-risk&quot; systems face mandatory conformity requirements and ex-ante assessment before they can reach the market, a narrow set of systems face transparency-only obligations, and everything else is unregulated apart from voluntary codes of conduct. Unlike the U.S. documents drafted for this course week, this is a Regulation — directly applicable law under Article 288 TFEU, chosen specifically &quot;for a uniform application of the new rules&quot; rather than an advisory report or an executive order.</p>",
