            "text": "- \"Anthropic, an AI safety and research company, has raised $124 million in a Series A.\"\n  The 2021 release's opening description of the company, with no account of its origin.\n\n- \"The Series A round was led by Jaan Tallinn, technology investor and co-founder of Skype.\"\n  Names the lead investor; the release never names a prior employer for the founders.\n\n- \"We founded Anthropic because we believe the impact of AI might be comparable to that of the industrial and scientific revolutions, but we aren't confident it will go well.\"\n  The 2023 essay's stated founding motive — belief about AI's trajectory, not an account of leaving anywhere.\n\n- \"We trained the first version of our headline model, Claude, in the spring of 2022, and decided to prioritize using it for safety research rather than public deployments.\"\n  What the 2023 essay chooses to narrate about Anthropic's early history, in plac"
