            "html": "<ul><li>&quot;Training machine learning models on publicly available data is considered fair use across the machine learning community.&quot;</li></ul><p>GitHub's claim that a community norm settles the training-data question.</p><ul><li>&quot;GitHub Copilot is a tool, like a compiler or a pen.&quot;</li></ul><p>GitHub's rhetoric placing the model among neutral instruments.</p><ul><li>&quot;The suggestions GitHub Copilot generates, and the code you write with its help, belong to you, and you are responsible for it.&quot;</li></ul><p>Ownership and liability both assigned to the user.</p><ul><li>&quot;In the future we will give users the option to control how their telemetry is used.&quot;</li></ul><p>Data collection on by default, control postponed.</p><ul><li>&quot;We want to use the preview to learn how people use GitHub Copilot and what it takes to operate it at scale.&quot;</li></ul><p>The preview as a use-stage experiment before commercialization.</p>",
