        "citation": "Friedman, Nat. 2021. \"Introducing GitHub Copilot: Your AI Pair Programmer.\" The GitHub Blog. June 29, 2021. https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/introducing-github-copilot-ai-pair-programmer/ Source used for this note: GitHub Copilot landing page and FAQ (copilot.github.com), Internet Archive snapshot of July 5, 2021.",
        "keyClaim": "GitHub launches a limited technical preview of GitHub Copilot, \"a new AI pair programmer\" that suggests whole lines or entire functions inside the code editor. It is built with OpenAI and runs on OpenAI Codex, which GitHub describes as more capable than GPT-3 at code generation because it was trained on much more public source code. The accompanying FAQ answers the questions GitHub expected: what it was trained on, whether it copies code, who owns the output, what data it collects, and what it means for developer jobs.",
