        "citation": "Coalition for Content Provenance and Authenticity. 2022. \"C2PA Releases Specification of World's First Industry Standard for Content Provenance.\" Press release. C2PA. January 26, 2022. https://c2pa.org/post/release_1_pr/",
        "keyClaim": "The Coalition for Content Provenance and Authenticity (C2PA) announces version 1.0 of its technical specification for digital provenance, which it calls the first industry standard of its kind. The specification defines how information about who created or changed a piece of digital content, and how it was altered, can be attached to images, video, audio and documents in a tamper-evident way. The coalition presents it as a response to the difficulty of trusting online content, naming \"deepfakes generated by artificial intelligence\" alongside traditionally manipulated media, and designs it as an opt-in open standard for software, devices, platforms and regulators to adopt.",
