            "title": "Historical References and Lineages",
            "html": "<ul><li>Before: Executive Order 13859 - Maintaining American Leadership in Artificial Intelligence (2019), an earlier non-binding federal AI instrument from the same executive branch; &quot;Recommendation on the Ethics of Artificial Intelligence&quot; (Nov 2021), a broader international values statement issued the year before.</li><li>After: NIST AI Risk Management Framework 1.0 (Jan 2023), another voluntary federal framework, using risk-management rather than rights language; China's Interim Measures for Generative AI Services (Aug 2023), a binding instrument issued the following year that enforces some of the same concerns — discrimination, transparency, user notice — through law rather than principle.</li></ul>",
            "text": "- Before: Executive Order 13859 - Maintaining American Leadership in Artificial Intelligence (2019), an earlier non-binding federal AI instrument from the same executive branch; \"Recommendation on the Ethics of Artificial Intelligence\" (Nov 2021), a broader international values statement issued the year before.\n- After: NIST AI Risk Management Framework 1.0 (Jan 2023), another voluntary federal framework, using risk-management rather than rights language; China's Interim Measures for Generative AI Services (Aug 2023), a binding instrument issued the following year that enforces some of the same concerns — discrimination, transparency, user notice — through law rather than principle."
