            "id": "why-this-matters",
            "title": "Why This Matters",
            "html": "<p>Read against Synthesis — AI as Technology History §4.6, the Blueprint is a state actor producing rights language at the exact point where Statutory Consolidation has not begun and, on the evidence of its own disappearance from its original host, may not follow at all. Its own text is unusually candid about this: every disclaimer paragraph in the Legal Disclaimer section says, in different words, that nothing here binds anyone. That candor is itself informative — it shows what an American state actor produces when it wants to be seen addressing a governance question without accepting the cost of actually deciding it.</p>",
