            "html": "<ul><li>The article depends on earlier histories of open-source software, internet collaboration, platform ecosystems, and personal computing.</li><li>It also connects to the history of statistical machine learning, deep learning scaling laws, GPU-based training, synthetic datasets, human feedback, and benchmark culture.</li><li>The analogy to Stable Diffusion is central: the article argues that open image-generation models showed how public model access could produce user interfaces, marketplaces, integrations, and cultural impact faster than a closed alternative.</li><li>The analogy is useful but partial. It captures the importance of openness and adaptation, but language models raised different stakes around search, work, knowledge production, safety, and platform control.</li></ul>",
            "text": "- The article depends on earlier histories of open-source software, internet collaboration, platform ecosystems, and personal computing.\n- It also connects to the history of statistical machine learning, deep learning scaling laws, GPU-based training, synthetic datasets, human feedback, and benchmark culture.\n- The analogy to Stable Diffusion is central: the article argues that open image-generation models showed how public model access could produce user interfaces, marketplaces, integrations, and cultural impact faster than a closed alternative.\n- The analogy is useful but partial. It captures the importance of openness and adaptation, but language models raised different stakes around search, work, knowledge production, safety, and platform control."
