            "html": "<ul><li>Before: Introducing LLaMA - A foundational 65-billion-parameter large language model, whose leak this memo treats as the triggering event — the memo's own timeline runs &quot;Feb 24, 2023 - LLaMA is Launched&quot; to &quot;March 3, 2023 - The Inevitable Happens.&quot; No direct after-note in this batch, though the memo's closing argument for Google to own the ecosystem anticipates a strategy the field later adopted.</li><li>This complicates Synthesis — AI as Technology History's §4.4 pairing of Technological Momentum and Unnatural Monopoly, which asks how much of frontier concentration is cost structure versus strategy. This memo argues, from inside Google, that by the spring of 2023 concentration had already stopped holding on its own — the strategic response, open up rather than fight it, came only after that.</li></ul>",
