        "citation": "Subcommittee on Privacy, Technology, and the Law, Committee on the Judiciary, United States Senate. 2023. \"Oversight of A.I.: Rules for Artificial Intelligence.\" S. Hrg. 118-037. May 16, 2023. https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-118shrg52706/html/CHRG-118shrg52706.htm",
        "keyClaim": "At the first in a planned series of hearings, the Subcommittee on Privacy, Technology, and the Law heard from OpenAI CEO Sam Altman, NYU professor emeritus Gary Marcus, and IBM chief privacy and trust officer Christina Montgomery on how, or whether, to regulate generative AI. The hearing is not a single position but a record of three different answers converging and diverging in real time: Altman and Marcus both endorse a licensing regime tied to a new federal agency, Montgomery argues against a new agency in favor of \"precision regulation\" of specific use cases, and several senators state they already have bills in progress that touch pieces of the problem, none of them a comprehensive AI s",
