            "html": "<p>Six Chinese state bodies jointly issue binding rules for generative AI services offered to the public in mainland China, imposing obligations on providers at each stage of the AI lifecycle — training data sourcing, content moderation, user agreements, labeling, and security review — enforced through warnings, corrections, service suspension, and referral for &quot;public security administrative sanction&quot; or criminal responsibility. A 2025 companion instrument, also translated by China Law Translate, adds detailed labeling requirements for AI-generated content.</p>",
            "text": "Six Chinese state bodies jointly issue binding rules for generative AI services offered to the public in mainland China, imposing obligations on providers at each stage of the AI lifecycle — training data sourcing, content moderation, user agreements, labeling, and security review — enforced through warnings, corrections, service suspension, and referral for \"public security administrative sanction\" or criminal responsibility. A 2025 companion instrument, also translated by China Law Translate, adds detailed labeling requirements for AI-generated content."
