            "text": "On October 30, 2023 the G7 leaders welcomed two documents, International Guiding Principles and an International Code of Conduct for organizations developing advanced AI systems, and called on those organizations \"to commit to the application of the International Code of Conduct.\" The Code offers \"voluntary guidance\" in eleven actions, applied \"in line with a risk-based approach\" across the AI lifecycle, covering pre-deployment testing, post-deployment monitoring, public transparency reports, incident sharing, security of model weights, content provenance, and technical standards. It describes itself as a \"living document\" that builds on the OECD AI Principles and asks firms to follow it \"while governments develop more enduring and/or detailed governance and regulatory approaches.\""
