            "id": "useful-quotes-evidence",
            "title": "Useful Quotes / Evidence",
            "html": "<ul><li>&quot;the first-ever international legally binding treaty in this field&quot;</li></ul><p>The Council's claim to priority.</p><ul><li>&quot;In order to stand the test of time, the Framework Convention does not regulate technology and is essentially technology-neutral.&quot;</li></ul><p>Regulation of uses, not of systems.</p><ul><li>&quot;Parties may opt to be directly obliged by the relevant Convention provisions or, as an alternative, take other measures&quot;</li></ul><p>Flexibility for the private sector.</p><ul><li>&quot;Possibility for the authorities to introduce ban or moratoria on certain application of AI systems (“red lines”).&quot;</li></ul><p>Bans allowed within the framework.</p><ul><li>&quot;The convention will not apply to national defence matters nor to research and development activities&quot;</li></ul><p>The treaty's main exclusions.</p>",
            "text": "- \"the first-ever international legally binding treaty in this field\"\n  The Council's claim to priority.\n- \"In order to stand the test of time, the Framework Convention does not regulate technology and is essentially technology-neutral.\"\n  Regulation of uses, not of systems.\n- \"Parties may opt to be directly obliged by the relevant Convention provisions or, as an alternative, take other measures\"\n  Flexibility for the private sector.\n- \"Possibility for the authorities to introduce ban or moratoria on certain application of AI systems (“red lines”).\"\n  Bans allowed within the framework.\n- \"The convention will not apply to national defence matters nor to research and development activities\"\n  The treaty's main exclusions."
