        "citation": "Leike, Jan. 2024. Resignation thread. X (formerly Twitter). May 17, 2024. https://x.com/janleike/status/1791498178346549382",
        "keyClaim": "Four executives left two frontier labs across twenty-seven months, each explaining the departure differently. Jan Leike, OpenAI's head of alignment and superalignment co-lead, posted a 13-part thread on May 17, 2024 stating he had been \"disagreeing with OpenAI leadership about the company's core priorities for quite some time.\" Miles Brundage, OpenAI's Senior Advisor for AGI Readiness, published a long, structured explanation on October 23, 2024, citing opportunity costs, a wish for independence, and a belief that \"neither OpenAI nor any other frontier lab is ready\" for AGI. Reuters reported in November 2025 that Yann LeCun, Meta's chief AI scientist, was leaving to start his own company aft",
