            "id": "why-this-matters",
            "title": "Why This Matters",
            "html": "<p>Read against Synthesis — AI as Technology History §4.6, the Frontier AI Safety Commitments are Corporate Self-regulation with a deadline rather than Statutory Consolidation: the same sixteen companies who count as &quot;frontier AI&quot; developers write the definition of frontier AI, set their own risk thresholds with government input reduced to &quot;as appropriate,&quot; and choose how much to disclose about outside involvement in assessing their own risk. The Seoul Declaration surrounding it broadens the stated public interest — diversity, digital divides, human rights — without attaching any new enforcement to the commitments it welcomes. Six months after Bletchley's high-water mark, this is still agenda-setting through commissioned practice rather than binding rule.</p>",
            "text": "Read against Synthesis — AI as Technology History §4.6, the Frontier AI Safety Commitments are Corporate Self-regulation with a deadline rather than Statutory Consolidation: the same sixteen companies who count as \"frontier AI\" developers write the definition of frontier AI, set their own risk thresholds with government input reduced to \"as appropriate,\" and choose how much to disclose about outside involvement in assessing their own risk. The Seoul Declaration surrounding it broadens the stated public interest — diversity, digital divides, human rights — without attaching any new enforcement to the commitments it welcomes. Six months after Bletchley's high-water mark, this is still agenda-setting through commissioned practice rather than binding rule."
