        "citation": "Vance, J. D. 2025. \"Remarks by the Vice President at the Artificial Intelligence Action Summit in Paris, France.\" The American Presidency Project. February 11, 2025. https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-the-vice-president-the-artificial-intelligence-action-summit-paris-france",
        "keyClaim": "Speaking at the Paris AI Action Summit, whose earlier iteration Vance says carried the title \"AI safety,\" Vice President Vance opens by rejecting that premise directly: he is here to talk about \"AI opportunity\" instead. He argues against \"excessive regulation,\" insists AI \"must remain free from ideological bias,\" criticizes EU rules by name, and frames safety regulation itself as a tool incumbents use against competitors, before closing with a call to build rather than restrict.",
