            "text": "- Closure: the October post declares the matter settled in the company's own terms — \"OpenAI has completed its recapitalization, simplifying its corporate structure\" — closing, for now, the multi-year public argument over whether OpenAI would convert away from nonprofit control. The close is corporate self-description, not a court ruling or statute; it is a claim that the argument is over, offered by one of the two parties who had the argument.\n- Statutory Consolidation: no federal statute governs what a nonprofit-controlled AGI lab is required to do; the constraint that shaped OpenAI's structure came instead from two state Attorneys General exercising oversight of a nonprofit's charitable assets. This is consolidation happening through negotiated settlement with sub-federal regulators rather than through legislation — the stage the vault's synthesis calls still open for AI, playing out "
