            "title": "Historical References and Lineages",
            "html": "<ul><li>Before: Mistral Large 3 is described as the company's &quot;first mixture-of-experts model since the seminal Mixtral series,&quot; explicitly placing this release inside Mistral's own product lineage rather than presenting it as a fresh start.</li><li>Also this week: Mistral 3's continued Apache 2.0 weight release sits alongside &quot;DeepSeek-V4-Pro model card&quot;'s continued MIT-licensed release, in contrast to &quot;Introducing Muse Spark&quot;'s closed API approach; all three are corporate responses to the same competitive period.</li><li>After: Leanstral 1.5, seven months later, narrows from general open-weight competition toward a specific product category (formal verification), a path not directly comparable to the general-purpose models the rest of the week covers.</li><li>The open-weight strategy generally traces back to the argument made in &quot;Open Source AI is the Path Forward&quot; and sits in the same lineage as Chinese AI has leveled up, and brought renewed focus on the open weight model shift.</li></ul>",
