            "text": "- \"All models are released under the Apache 2.0 license\"\n  The licensing commitment stated at the top of the announcement, covering the entire Mistral 3 family.\n\n- \"Mistral Large 3 is one of the best permissive open weight models in the world, trained from scratch on 3000 of NVIDIA's H200 GPUs\"\n  The headline technical and infrastructure claim for the flagship model.\n\n- \"Delivering advanced open-source AI models requires broad optimization, achieved through a partnership with NVIDIA\"\n  The post's own account of where deployment efficiency actually comes from.\n\n- \"The future of AI is open\"\n  The announcement's closing framing, stated as description rather than as one company's strategic choice.\n\n- \"uncovers previously unknown bugs in open-source repositories\"\n  Leanstral 1.5's headline claim about applying formal verification to real-world code, from its own summary line."
