        "keyClaim": "Mistral AI announces Mistral 3, a family of models released under the Apache 2.0 license spanning three small dense models (14B, 8B, 3B, marketed as Ministral 3) and Mistral Large 3, a sparse Mixture-of-Experts model with 41B active and 675B total parameters. The post frames the release around open access and hardware partnership — a joint effort with NVIDIA, vLLM, and Red Hat to make the models efficient to deploy — and states plainly that \"the future of AI is open.\" The later Leanstral 1.5 update, also Apache 2.0 and also open-weighted, reports state-of-the-art results on formal theorem-proving benchmarks, treating automated proof engineering as its own product line rather than a side capa",
