        "keyClaim": "Building explicitly on EO 14179, this order moves from persuasion and funding hints to direct confrontation with state AI laws. It creates a Justice Department litigation task force to challenge state statutes in court, conditions a share of federal broadband funding on states repealing \"onerous\" AI laws, and directs the FTC and FCC to open proceedings aimed at federal preemption — all while separately asking Congress to pass the uniform national standard the order says does not yet exist. The order's published URL slug — eliminating-state-law-obstruction-of-national-artificial-intelligence-policy — is blunter than its official title.",
