            "id": "core-claim",
            "title": "Core Claim",
            "html": "<p>The model card presents DeepSeek-V4-Pro, a 1.6-trillion-parameter Mixture-of-Experts model with 49 billion parameters activated per token, alongside a smaller DeepSeek-V4-Flash variant, both supporting one-million-token context windows. The card's central technical claim is a hybrid attention architecture combining Compressed Sparse Attention and Heavily Compressed Attention that, at one-million-token context, cuts single-token inference compute to 27% and key-value cache to 10% of what DeepSeek-V3.2 required. The weights are released under the MIT license with full download links on Hugging Face and ModelScope, continuing the open-weight distribution model of the earlier V3 release while reporting benchmark parity with closed frontier systems including Opus, GPT, and Gemini.</p>",
            "text": "The model card presents DeepSeek-V4-Pro, a 1.6-trillion-parameter Mixture-of-Experts model with 49 billion parameters activated per token, alongside a smaller DeepSeek-V4-Flash variant, both supporting one-million-token context windows. The card's central technical claim is a hybrid attention architecture combining Compressed Sparse Attention and Heavily Compressed Attention that, at one-million-token context, cuts single-token inference compute to 27% and key-value cache to 10% of what DeepSeek-V3.2 required. The weights are released under the MIT license with full download links on Hugging Face and ModelScope, continuing the open-weight distribution model of the earlier V3 release while reporting benchmark parity with closed frontier systems including Opus, GPT, and Gemini."
