            "text": "- \"A jury in California took less than two hours to decide that Elon Musk waited too long to file a lawsuit against his one-time business partner Sam Altman\"\n  The core procedural finding.\n\n- \"In determining that the suit was filed too late, the jury sidestepped questions at the heart of Musk's case\"\n  States directly that the merits were never reached.\n\n- \"The finding of the jury confirms that what this lawsuit was a hypocritical attempt to sabotage a competitor and to overcome a long history of very bad predictions about what OpenAI has been and will become\"\n  OpenAI's lawyer claiming vindication.\n\n- \"This one is not over\"\n  Musk's attorney's response, claiming the fight continues despite the dismissal.\n\n- \"By 2017, the founders were convinced they needed to set up a for-profit arm of OpenAI to raise money and attract researchers in order to be competitive.\"\n  The origin of the structu"
