        "citation": "Ruwitch, John. 2026. \"Jury Dismisses All Claims in Elon Musk's Lawsuit Against OpenAI CEO Sam Altman.\" NPR. May 18, 2026. https://www.npr.org/2026/05/18/nx-s1-5822366/musk-altman-openai-jury-verdict-claims-dismissed.",
        "keyClaim": "An advisory jury in the Northern District of California finds, in under two hours, that Elon Musk waited too long to sue Sam Altman and OpenAI over the direction of the company since their 2018 falling out; Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers accepts the finding and dismisses the case on statute-of-limitations grounds. The article reports that the jury \"sidestepped questions at the heart of Musk's case\" — whether Altman and Brockman breached a charitable trust — so the substantive dispute over OpenAI's founding mission is never ruled on, and both sides publicly claim the outcome as vindication.",
