            "id": "why-this-matters",
            "title": "Why This Matters",
            "html": "<p>This is a short article doing a specific kind of work: converting an unaudited projection into a comparative fact that can carry an IPO valuation argument. The source itself supplies the caution — the companies may not be measuring the same thing — but that caution sits in one sentence while the headline and lede treat the number as settled. For the vault's history-of-technology argument, this is a small, current instance of how a contested figure gets naturalized into common sense before the underlying disagreement about its construction is even investigated, let alone resolved. Two record-setting numbers are being used to establish which AI company is ahead in the market, at a moment when what &quot;annualized revenue run rate&quot; means has not been standardized between the two companies using the phrase.</p>",
